@@ -9,6 +9,15 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Privacy audit
+
+- Account forms collect only a username and password, disclose the external demo authentication recipient before submission, and recommend made-up credentials. Requests omit cookies and referrers, disable caching, and reject redirects. Passwords are cleared after every attempt; backend response details and tokens are not read or persisted.
+- The shared layout loads no third-party analytics, ad scripts, or remote fonts. System fonts replace Google Fonts. Any future third-party integration needs a fresh review of its data flow and purpose, particularly on account pages.
+- HTML responses send `Referrer-Policy: no-referrer`, disable unused powerful features through `Permissions-Policy`, and set `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`. Account documents also send `Cache-Control: no-store`. A referrer meta tag preserves the policy during client navigation. Browsing no longer initializes an empty reading-list session.
+- The privacy page explains current behavior and limitations. External authentication retention, deletion/export support, and hosting log retention remain unverified. Real accounts require resolving those gaps. Existing external article images and article-specific debugging cookies are disclosed; this audit does not establish site-wide compliance or audit the external service.
+
+Run the privacy regression tests with Node 22.18+ using `node --test tests/privacy.test.mjs`, and compile with `pnpm run build`. Tests mock authentication requests and do not contact the external service. No browser or running application server is required.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
